DevOps Interview Q&A Series — Advanced Edition 🌟

Here’s a handpicked list of Kubernetes, Docker, CI/CD, and Terraform questions that you should definitely prepare 👇

🔹 Kubernetes
  How do Kubernetes components interact when you run kubectl apply?
  Explain Kubernetes architecture.
  How do you securely manage secrets in AKS using Azure Key Vault and CSI drivers?
 You’re hitting a Load Balancer URL and getting 503 errors, but Pods are running fine internally — how do you troubleshoot?
 StatefulSet vs Deployment — when do you use each?
 How can you restrict communication between 2 Pods in the same namespace?

🔹 Docker & Pipelines
 CMD vs ENTRYPOINT vs RUN in Docker.
 Difference between Docker Volumes and Bind Mounts (and which one works in K8s).
 Techniques to cache Docker layers or NPM/NuGet packages in pipelines.
 Rollback strategies you’ve implemented in production.
 Compliance as Code — how do you enforce policies, scanning, and security checks in CI/CD?

🔹 Terraform
 Purpose and real-world use cases of lifecycle blocks (prevent_destroy, create_before_destroy).
What happens internally when you run terraform init, plan, and apply?
How do you set up a remote backend in Azure (Blob storage) with state locking?
How do you manage Terraform state in a team environment?
How do you structure Terraform for multiple environments (Dev, QA, Prod)?
How do you modularize Terraform, and what pitfalls have you seen?
Scenario: Terraform state file is corrupted — how do you recover?
How do you test Terraform code before applying to production?

✨ These are not just theory-based — they’re real-world scenarios you will face as a DevOps Engineer.
